# nodejs — a real "floor-fixable? no" case from #6's own in/out taxonomy
# (category 3: "absolute data path baked in, needs overlay"). Tested
# the whole ladder rather than assumed:
#   - `node -e '...'` with zero env: fails, can't find libnode.so.137
#     (needs LD_LIBRARY_PATH — that part IS floor-fixable).
#   - with LD_LIBRARY_PATH set: node itself loads, then crashes loading
#     "internal/deps/undici/undici" from the hardcoded
#     /usr/share/nodejs/undici/undici-fetch.js — a path node's build baked
#     in, not a dynamic-linker lookup, so no env var reaches it.
#   - through tools/prefix-run.sh (overlay, $PREFIX/usr stacked on the
#     host's /usr): works. That absolute path resolves once /usr/share
#     itself is the prefix's copy, which only the overlay can do.
# So nodejs needs the next tier up — not floor, not a bug in check-package.sh
# either (its runtime=direct verdict was about node's own /usr/bin script
# content, not this internal builtin-loader path).
package  nodejs
install  risky
mechanism  overlay
verify   tools/prefix-run.sh node -e process.version
note     needs overlay, not floor — hardcoded /usr/share/nodejs/undici path, not an LD_LIBRARY_PATH gap
